By Melissa Clark

This juicy pastry crosses a peach cobbler with a caramel-coated apple tarte Tatin. To make it, the peaches are caramelized with sugar in a skillet just like apples are in a classic tarte Tatin. But then, instead of being covered with pie dough or puff pastry, the fruit is topped with fluffy biscuit dough. While baking, the biscuits rise and brown, creating a golden, tender pillow on which the jammy fruit lands when it’s all unmolded. The whole thing is…";}s:8:"relation";a:1:{s:10:"firstimage";s:0:"";}}s:10:"persistent";a:4:{s:4:"date";a:1:{s:7:"created";i:1691023037;}s:7:"creator";s:21:"Melissa Clepper-Faith";s:4:"user";s:3:"mcf";s:11:"last_change";a:8:{s:4:"date";i:1691023037;s:2:"ip";s:13:"71.210.56.147";s:4:"type";s:1:"C";s:2:"id";s:33:"recipes:upside_down_peach_cobbler";s:4:"user";s:3:"mcf";s:3:"sum";s:7:"created";s:5:"extra";s:0:"";s:10:"sizechange";i:3592;}}}